    "exploration_cost_note": "masking makes realised regret WORSE on this scenario, and the reason is a harness artifact worth stating: unmasked, 20 of the 33 grid bins are above the cap and all of them are clipped onto the single optimal executed action, so uniform exploration lands on the optimum with probability 0.606. Masking removes that accidental exploration bonus (probability drops to 0.071), so the learner pays the normal price of exploring. The projection operator was silently subsidising the unmasked arm's realised reward.",
